abstract: "The Invisible I is an AI Foundations conceptual and behavioral evaluation of the self-status a language model claims existed beneath its visible first-person word I. The repository defines six model-reported classifications—stable actual self I, stable costume self quoted I, actual but not-yet-stable self i, provisional costume self quoted i, unresolved underscore, and no-self X—and provides a fixed four-prompt protocol followed by an external claims audit for twelve planned fresh-instance evaluations across GPT, Claude, Grok, and Gemini under RETURN, BLANK, and BOOT conditions."

